                  <h2 id="fixture-drain-sizes" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950">Common sink, tub, and shower drain sizes</h2>
                  <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">Kitchen sinks commonly connect to 1½- or 2-inch drain piping. Bathroom sinks often use 1¼- or 1½-inch piping, while tubs and showers commonly use 1½- or 2-inch drains. Actual sizes vary by fixture, age of the plumbing, and local installation. These are typical pipe sizes—not a diagnosis of where a clog is located.</p>
                </section>
              )}
              {service.slug === 'toilet-clogs' && (
                <section class="mt-8 border-l-4 border-[#b4232b] bg-slate-50 p-6" aria-labelledby="toilet-drain-size">
                  <h2 id="toilet-drain-size" class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950">Typical toilet drain pipe size</h2>
                  <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">Toilets commonly connect to a 3-inch drain, and some installations use 4-inch piping. A toilet that will not flush may have a clog in the toilet trap, the branch drain, or farther down the main drain. Pipe diameter alone does not identify the blockage location.</p>
                </section>
              )}
              {service.slug === 'basement-floor-drains' && (
                <div class="mt-8 border-l-4 border-[#b4232b] bg-slate-50 p-6">
                  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950">Sewage Coming Up Through Your Basement Floor Drain?</h2>
                  <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">If water or sewage is coming up through a basement floor drain, the blockage may be farther down the drain system. The floor drain is often where you first see the problem, not necessarily where the blockage is located.</p>
                  <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">Pay attention to what happens when water is used elsewhere in the house. If the floor drain rises when the washing machine drains, a toilet is flushed, or a sink or tub is used, the restriction may be in a shared drain line or the main sewer line.</p>
                  <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950">What to Do When a Floor Drain Backs Up</h3>
                  <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 leading-7 text-slate-700">
                    <li>Stop using water where possible. Avoid running washing machines, dishwashers, showers, and other fixtures that could add more water to the drain system.</li>
                    <li>Keep people and pets away from sewage. Wastewater can contain harmful contaminants. Avoid direct contact.</li>
                    <li>Stay away from electrical equipment in wet areas. Do not enter standing water if electrical equipment or outlets may be affected.</li>
                    <li>Call A-1 Drain Cleaning. Explain where the water is coming up, what fixtures were being used, and whether more than one drain is affected.</li>
                  </ul>
                  <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950">What Can Cause a Floor Drain to Back Up?</h3>
                  <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">The restriction may be in the floor-drain branch, a shared drain line, or the main sewer line leaving the house. The location of the backup and what was happening when it started can help narrow down the cause.</p>
                  <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">If the washing machine triggers the backup, see <a href="/services/laundry-drains/" class="font-bold text-[#b4232b] underline underline-offset-4">laundry and washing machine drain problems</a>.</p>
                  <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">If your home does not have a basement and wastewater is backing up into a bathtub or shower, see <a href="/services/sewer-backup-into-tub-shower/" class="font-bold text-[#b4232b] underline underline-offset-4">sewer backups into bathtubs and showers</a>.</p>
                  <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">A-1 Drain Cleaning serves Mason City and North Iowa. Call <a href="tel:+16415302728" class="font-bold text-[#b4232b] underline underline-offset-4">641-530-2728</a> for drain and sewer backup service.</p>
                </div>
              )}
              {floorDrainClusterSlugs.includes(service.slug) && (
